      "body": "## Motivation\n\nA `FROZEN_KV_MTP` draft (the Gemma-4 assistant) reads the target KV pool and owns no per-token KV; its own runner pool is a 64-token placeholder. But `is_eagle()` includes it, so the pool configurators add its layers to the per-token cell size and shrink the target pool for KV nobody allocates.\n\nOn Gemma-4-31B (hybrid SWA, 4-layer draft) the full-attention pool is 11.8% smaller than it needs to be at `--swa-full-tokens-ratio 0.2`. Unlike the EAGLE/STANDALONE accounting added in #28219, a frozen draft has no pool of its own to pay for.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Add `_target_pays_for_draft_kv()` in `pool_configurator.py`. It replaces the duplicated `is_eagle() or is_standalone()` gate in the default and hybrid-SWA configurators and returns False for `FROZEN_KV_MTP`.\n- Keep the charge under `--enable-unified-memory`: the draft worker builds a pool over the virtual id space there.\n- `is_eagle()` and its FIXME are untouched.\n- Add `TestFrozenKvMtpDraftBudget` (4 cases) to `test_pool_configurator.py`.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nCapacity-only change; the forward path is untouched. GSM8K, full set, `sgl-eval run gsm8k` (temperature 0, seed 42, `--no-thinking`, max 2048 tokens, 32 threads), triton, 1×H200:\n\n| | Score | Correct / Total |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| main | 97.04% | 1,280 / 1,319 |\n| this PR | 96.97% | 1,279 / 1,319 |\n\n0 errors and 0 truncated outputs in both runs.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nStartup pool size, 1×H200, `RedHatAI/gemma-4-31B-it-FP8-block` + `google/gemma-4-31B-it-assistant`, TP1, `--mem-fraction-static 0.92 --swa-full-tokens-ratio 0.2 --context-length 262144 --max-running-requests 16 --chunked-prefill-size 8192 --attention-backend triton --speculative-algorithm NEXTN --speculative-num-steps 4 --speculative-eagle-topk 1 --speculative-num-draft-tokens 5`:\n\n| | `full_layer_tokens` | `swa_layer_tokens` |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| main | 365,679 | 73,135 |\n| this PR | 414,436 (+13.3%) | 82,887 |\n\n`fa4` gives the same pool sizes. No serving throughput is claimed. Image: `lmsysorg/sglang:dev` (`sha256:b5c488694d74c13587af6057b90220498c4869571c8e1e3c43dd6f43ae721306`) with `python/` overlaid from `origin/main` @ `130e11d50e` and from this PR.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the Format code with pre-commit.\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the Run and add unit tests.\n- [ ] Update documentation according to Write documentations. (no user-facing change)\n- [x] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to Test the accuracy and Benchmark the speed.\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style guidance.\n\nNote: `fa4` with `FROZEN_KV_MTP` crashes on `main` under load (illegal memory access), with or without this PR (likely #43542).\n\ncc @hnyls2002 @Qiaolin-Yu @kpham-sgl @pyc96\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38245717002](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38245717002)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38245716737](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38245716737)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38245716934](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38245716934)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
